{"agent_id":"pp3g-2Gfr-research-read-only-investigate-opencode-s-plugin-hook","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T02:26:28.944958985Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"32e370bd-e3f2-430f-ae77-28b0afca8694","comment_uuid":"c76fa9f0-b82e-4451-8884-95c35f59716e","author":"pp3g-2Gfr-research-read-only-investigate-opencode-s-plugin-hook","content":"# RESEARCH RESULT — OpenCode plugin/hook system for a \"documentation-check-before-consequential-action\" hook\n\n**Sources (all read-only, no files modified):**\n- Fork source preserved in-repo: `fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts` (the `Hooks` interface), `packages/opencode/src/{session/tools.ts, session/prompt.ts, session/llm/request.ts, plugin/index.ts, plugin/loader.ts, config/config.ts, config/plugin.ts, tool/registry.ts, permission/…}`, `packages/sdk/js/src/gen/{types,sdk}.gen.ts`\n- Live binary: `opencode 1.18.13-pp3g-fork` at `~/.nvm/.../opencode-ai/bin/opencode.exe` (fork identity guard in `~/.local/bin/opencode`)\n- In-repo plugins: `.opencode/plugins/{crosslink-guard,orchestrator-guard,rtk-guard}.ts`, `.opencode/opencode.json`, `.opencode/design/rtk-guard-plugin-design.md`\n- Upstream docs: https://opencode.ai/docs/plugins/ (Aug 17 2026)\n- Prior art: `docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md`, `docs/research/harness-evaluations/2026-07-12-rtk-opencode-gap-analysis.md`\n\n---\n\n## 1. Full enumeration of plugin hook events (fork 1.18.13-pp3g-fork)\n\n`@opencode-ai/plugin` exports type `Plugin = (input: PluginInput, options?) => Promise<Hooks>`. `PluginInput` = `{ client (opencode SDK), project, directory, worktree, experimental_workspace, serverUrl, $ (BunShell) }`. The complete `Hooks` interface (`fork/opencode-src/packages/plugin/src/index.ts:222-335`):\n\n| Hook | Input (what it receives) | Output (mutable) | Fires when / notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `event` | `{ event: Event }` — union of ~30 session events (`message.updated`, `session.status`, `session.idle`, `command.executed`, `permission.asked`, `file.edited`, `todo.updated`, …) | — | Every session event; fire-and-forget, hook errors are swallowed (`plugin/index.ts:253-259`) |\n| `config` | merged `Config` | — | Once at plugin init |\n| `tool` | — | custom tool definitions | Plugin-defined custom tools |\n| `auth` / `provider` | provider/auth context | auth methods / models | Auth & provider hooks |\n| `chat.message` | `{ sessionID, agent?, model?, messageID?, variant? }` | `{ message: UserMessage, parts: Part[] }` — parts MUTABLE | Each user message received (`session/prompt.ts:1004`); used by guards to learn agent name per session |\n| `chat.params` | `{ sessionID, agent, model, provider: ProviderContext, message: UserMessage }` | `{ temperature, topP, topK, maxOutputTokens, options }` | Each LLM request (`session/llm/request.ts:114`) |\n| `chat.headers` | same as chat.params | `{ headers }` | Each LLM request (`request.ts:134`) |\n| `permission.ask` | `Permission` | `{ status: \"ask\"\\|\"deny\"\\|\"allow\" }` | **DECLARED but NEVER triggered anywhere in the fork** — dead hook, do not rely on it |\n| `command.execute.before` | `{ command, sessionID, arguments }` | `{ parts: Part[] }` — MUTABLE | **Slash commands only** (TUI `/foo`), `session/prompt.ts:1465`. NOT fired for Bash tool calls |\n| `tool.execute.before` | `{ tool, sessionID, callID }` | `{ args: any }` — MUTABLE | Every tool call incl. bash/write/edit/read/task and MCP tools (`session/tools.ts:106,176,259,339,403`; `prompt.ts:312` for the `task` subagent tool) |\n| `shell.env` | `{ cwd, sessionID?, callID? }` | `{ env }` | Before any shell execution (`plugin/pty-environment.ts:18`); can inject env vars into ALL shell calls |\n| `tool.execute.after` | `{ tool, sessionID, callID, args }` | `{ title, output, metadata }` | After each tool call; can rewrite the tool result shown to the model |\n| `experimental.chat.messages.transform` | `{}` | `{ messages: {info, parts}[] }` | Per-request, before messages go to the LLM (`prompt.ts:1259`, `compaction.ts:350`) |\n| `experimental.chat.system.transform` | `{ sessionID?, model }` | `{ system: string[] }` — push to append | Per-request system-prompt build (`request.ts:70`, `agent.ts:381`) — **direct model-context injection channel** |\n| `experimental.provider.small_model` | `{ provider }` | `{ model? }` | Small-model selection |\n| `experimental.session.compacting` | `{ sessionID }` | `{ context: string[], prompt? }` | Before compaction; push context strings |\n| `experimental.compaction.autocontinue` | `{ sessionID, agent, model, provider, message, overflow }` | `{ enabled }` | After compaction |\n| `experimental.text.complete` | `{ sessionID, messageID, partID }` | `{ text }` | Streaming text completion |\n| `tool.definition` | `{ toolID }` | `{ description, parameters }` | Tool resolution (`tool/registry.ts:313`); can rewrite the bash/read tool descriptions the model sees |\n\n**Blocking mechanic (verified):** a hook that `throw new Error(msg)` fails the plugin `Effect.promise`, aborting the tool call; the AI SDK emits a `tool-error` whose `message` = the thrown error text, which the model receives as the tool result (`session/llm/ai-sdk.ts:249-262`). This is exactly how crosslink-guard's \"MANDATORY COMPLIANCE\" blocks reach the model.\n\n## 2. How the existing guard plugins use the API\n\n- **crosslink-guard.ts** (`.opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts`): on `tool.execute.before`, filters `write|edit|bash`; blocks/gates by parsing `output.args.command` (git blocklists, gated `git commit` w/ active-issue + `--kind plan` comment discipline via `bun:sqlite` on `.crosslink/issues.db`), allowlists bash prefixes, shells out to `crosslink agent flags --strict` / `session status` via BunShell `$`. Agent identity per sessionID from `chat.params`/`chat.message` (fixes #204 clobbering). Block = `throw new Error(...)`; allow = return; config from `.crosslink/hook-config.json` + `.local` overlay.\n- **orchestrator-guard.ts**: same hook; throws for `write|edit|apply_patch|filesystem_write_file|filesystem_edit_file` unless session agent is `builder`.\n- **rtk-guard.ts**: same hook; **mutates** `output.args.command` (bash) to prepend `rtk`; strictly fail-open; loop guard; latency gate.\n- Registration: `.opencode/opencode.json` `plugin` array lists all three, AND `.opencode/plugin(s)/*.ts` are auto-discovered via `Glob.scan(\"{plugin,plugins}/*.{ts,js}\")` (`config/plugin.ts:18-30`), deduped on exact file URL (`deduplicatePluginOrigins`). So a new plugin in `.opencode/plugins/` needs **no config change**.\n- Load order: global config → project config → global plugins → project plugins; within a dir the observed (not API-guaranteed) order is alphabetical by filename; hooks run sequentially in registration order.\n\n## 3. Can a hook fire before kickoff/swarm dispatch or hook-config.json edits? YES — via `tool.execute.before` + command/file matching\n\n- **`crosslink kickoff run` / `crosslink swarm launch` are dispatched as Bash tool calls**, not slash commands (kickoff skill: \"Execute `crosslink kickoff run` with all flags\"; `.claude/skills/kickoff/SKILL.md:67`). Therefore `command.execute.before` does NOT fire for them; the intercept point is `tool.execute.before` with `tool === \"bash\"`, parsing `output.args.command` — exactly the pattern crosslink-guard already uses for git commands. Match e.g. `/crosslink\\s+kickoff\\s+run/`, `/crosslink\\s+swarm\\s+launch/`, `/crosslink\\s+kickoff\\s+status/` as needed.\n- **Also interceptable: opencode-native subagent dispatch** — the built-in `task` tool fires `tool.execute.before` with `tool: \"task\"` and args `{ prompt, description, subagent_type, command }` (`session/prompt.ts:305-315`). A doc-check gate can target either or both surfaces.\n- **hook-config.json edits** are `write`/`edit` tool calls with `output.args.filePath` (crosslink-guard already reads this field for the `~/.claude/` exemption); MCP `filesystem_write_file`/`filesystem_edit_file` are also visible in the same hook (orchestrator-guard already matches them).\n- **What a hook can inject / do** (all proven by existing code):\n  1. **Block + instruct**: throw an Error whose text tells the agent to read the knowledge page first (or embeds the page's key content). The text becomes the tool-error the model reads — this is the *de facto* \"inject into model context\" mechanism the guards already rely on.\n  2. **Rewrite the command**: mutate `output.args.command`, e.g. prepend `cat .crosslink/knowledge/agent-orchestration-playbook.md && ` so the doc content lands in the tool result before the consequential action runs (rtk-guard proves arg mutation works).\n  3. **Persistent system-prompt injection**: `experimental.chat.system.transform` → `output.system.push(...)` appends to the system prompt on every request (global, not per-action).\n  4. **Tool-description injection**: `tool.definition` can append doc-check guidance to the `bash` tool's description.\n  5. **Per-command parts injection**: `command.execute.before` `output.parts` — but only for slash commands, so not the kickoff path.\n- **Can a plugin read a knowledge page? YES.** Knowledge pages are plain markdown under `.crosslink/knowledge/*.md` (4 pages today: agent-orchestration-playbook.md, crosslink-fork.md, kickoff-custom-template.md, model-discipline.md). Plugins run in Bun with full `node:fs`/`bun:sqlite` access and the plugin's `directory` (project root); crosslink-guard already reads `.crosslink/hook-config.json`, `.active-issue`, and `issues.db` directly.\n\n## 4. Doc-read confirmation — how to prove \"the agent read the page first\"\n\nFour workable mechanisms (the last is the most consistent with existing repo discipline):\n1. **Per-session in-memory tracking**: record `tool.execute.before` calls where `tool === \"read\"` and `output.args.filePath` ends with the required page; consult the map when the kickoff command arrives. Cheap, but lost on process restart.\n2. **SDK history query**: the plugin's `client.session.messages({ path: { id: sessionID } })` lists the session's messages (sdk.gen.ts:603) — scan for a prior read of the page.\n3. **Sentinel file**: require `touch .crosslink/.doc-read-<page>` (or a crosslink subcommand) before the action is allowed.\n4. **Crosslink comment-kind discipline (recommended)**: mirror the existing plan/result discipline — require a `--kind observation`/`plan` comment on the active issue that acks the doc (regex e.g. `read:agent-orchestration-playbook`), checked via `bun:sqlite` on `.crosslink/issues.db` exactly like `issueHasCommentKind` in crosslink-guard (lines 665-687). This reuses the proven durability + audit-trail path.\n\n## 5. Concrete recommendation — where the doc-check hook would live\n\n- **New plugin file**: `.opencode/plugins/doc-check-guard.ts` (auto-discovered; no `.opencode/opencode.json` edit required; add explicit entry only if ordering control is wanted — array order is respected before directory scan order per config merge).\n- **Hook**: `tool.execute.before` only.\n- **Intercepts**: (a) `tool === \"bash\"` and `output.args.command` matches `crosslink kickoff run` / `crosslink swarm launch`; optionally (b) `tool === \"write\"|\"edit\"|\"filesystem_write_file\"|\"filesystem_edit_file\"` with filePath resolving to `.crosslink/hook-config.json` (and `opencode.json` if desired); optionally (c) `tool === \"task\"` (native subagent dispatch).\n- **Policy config**: extend `.crosslink/hook-config.json` with a `doc_check` block, e.g. `{ \"required_before\": { \"crosslink kickoff run\": [\"agent-orchestration-playbook\"], \"crosslink swarm launch\": [\"agent-orchestration-playbook\"], \".crosslink/hook-config.json\": [\"crosslink-fork\"] } }` — same single-config-source pattern the guards already use (`loadConfigMerged`).\n- **Behavior**: if the required page hasn't been acked (mechanism §4.4), `throw new Error(...)` with the page path + a one-line summary + the exact ack command (e.g. `crosslink issue comment <id> \"read:agent-orchestration-playbook\" --kind observation`). Ordering note: `doc-check-guard.ts` sorts after `crosslink-guard.ts`, but that is fine because crosslink-guard *allows* `crosslink *` commands (allowed_bash_prefixes) without throwing, so the doc-check hook still runs; rtk-guard never rewrites `crosslink *` (V1_VALIDATED = git/ls/grep/find/diff/wc/cat), so no rewrite interop hazard.\n- **Alternative (smaller footprint)**: extend crosslink-guard.ts with a `doc_check` section instead of a new file — avoids a fourth plugin and inherits the config-loading/agent-tracking machinery, at the cost of coupling.\n\n## 6. Limitations & caveats\n\n1. **`permission.ask` is unusable**: declared in the Hooks type but no `plugin.trigger(\"permission.ask\", …)` exists in the fork — the deny/allow path is not wired.\n2. **`command.execute.before` will NOT catch kickoff/swarm** — it fires only for slash commands; the bash-command path is the only intercept for `crosslink kickoff run`.\n3. **`experimental.*` hooks are unstable by contract** — system/messages transform names can change across versions; treat as enhancement, not the gate.\n4. **Fork-version pinning**: findings are against `1.18.13-pp3g-fork`; stock/upstream may differ. The in-repo source copy (`fork/opencode-src`) is the authoritative reference; `opencode` upstream docs list the same core hooks (plugins doc, Aug 17 2026) plus event subscriptions.\n5. **Hook ordering is observed, not guaranteed** — a future opencode change could reorder plugin execution; a doc-check plugin must tolerate running before/after crosslink-guard (fail-closed only on its own matches).\n6. **Block message is the only reliable injection** — the thrown Error text is what the model reads; full knowledge-page content in the message is possible but should be truncated (context cost); command-rewrite injection (`cat page && …`) alters the executed command and needs a loop guard + rtk-style attestation.\n7. **MCP tool args differ** — `filesystem_write_file` etc. carry `path`, not `filePath`; the plugin must handle both shapes (orchestrator-guard matches by tool name only).\n8. **Subagent sessions share the process** — agent identity and doc-read state must be keyed by sessionID (the #204 lesson), or a reviewer subagent's reads could satisfy the parent's gate.\n\n**WHAT-NOT-TESTED**: no live smoke test of a doc-check plugin was run (read-only task); `client.session.messages()` was verified to exist in the generated SDK but not exercised from inside a plugin; hook ordering within `.opencode/plugins/` was not re-verified empirically this session (prior evidence: rtk-guard design doc §Appendix C).","created_at":"2026-08-18T02:26:28.938209418Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:NoFKIm/eAclBeXJFToi3i1IZsGu87l9De+yIxG4gDW4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgScvMpgXnyqKazUcdfM0VWpw7fpKUNzHbKifwDi5Dr/wAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA6PNY+pm5d6NlGV/Ok8jmI8iXdOZDf2rBoV6CB+Us4h3hhzShJuJto9rNBdtgBDtZr0oLnM/PP2ABHSaOoRixDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:NoFKIm/eAclBeXJFToi3i1IZsGu87l9De+yIxG4gDW4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgScvMpgXnyqKazUcdfM0VWpw7fpKUNzHbKifwDi5Dr/wAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAivF1OMdT2BGtkMnfCvgT5m2U9Wpfdaj7WvOGarvsWDhAHhpjiV846rKnSquvOkZuZB8DDZJKfCi9Z5/cIdzQs="}
